# The Mathlib slice's roots (scripts/mathlib-slice.py; docs/design/MATHLIB_FRONT.md
# section 6, slice B of its measurements): real numbers, add_zero, add_comm and
# what the front end's searches need. One declaration name per line, as Lean
# prints it; scripts/export-slice.py adds everything they need.
add_zero
add_comm
Real
Real.instAdd
Real.instZero
Real.instAddMonoid
Real.instAddCommSemigroup
AddMonoid.toAddZeroClass
AddCommSemigroup.toAddCommMagma
Zero.toOfNat0
instHAdd
instOfNatNat
# The candidate Lean's order tries first for OfNat ?α 0, HAdd ?α ?β ?γ, Add ?α and
# Zero ?α: without them a search with an unknown type meets an instance the
# slice left out and answers unsupported (the measurements' run 11).
Lean.Grind.CommRing.OfCommSemiring.instOfNatQ
Std.Time.WallTime.instHAddOffset_1
Lean.Grind.CommRing.OfCommSemiring.instAddQ
Pi.instZero
